Why not settle the issue once and for all? Submit pudding farming as a
bug report to the devteam. Suggest code to fix it if you like. Watch
the nethack.org buglist and wait for a definitive[1] answer.

FWIW, I think pudding farming is OK as it is. It's the kind of trick
only well-spoiled, fairly experienced players are going to try, and
most of them will soon get bored of it. The introduction of the
farmbot did expose just how cheesy farming is, but I don't mind a
little camembert, especially if I can just leave it at the side of the
plate untouched.[2]

Nevertheless, I once suggested my own fix, which I see as something of
a compromise between the two camps: Leave farming in, but give
puddings some kind of added attack or ability that increases their
deadliness in proportion to the size of the pud-herd. For example,
allowing them to re-merge into ultra-deadly megapuddings that are
significantly more dangerous than the sum of their parts. This adds a
risk to offset the reward while helping to alleviate the tedium for
those who persist, and makes the use of bots decidely risky. It makes
no significant changes to play balance for those people choose not to
farm/ have never heard of farming.




